        "module": "political-reformers",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[witness, frame]",
        "section": "political-reformers",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Witness's Frame",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "11. BUFFER SIZES\n      (stabilizers, reserves, shock absorbers)\n      ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n      Constitutional entrenchment: Bill of Rights, Basic Law,\n      habeas corpus. Buffers against tyranny of the moment.\n      FDR's Social Security: a financial buffer that created its\n      own political constituency (beneficiaries vote to protect it)."
    },
